SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Marina\, Flambouro
LOCATION:Flambouro (Apollonia area)\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Agia Marina that Sifniots go to is the chapel at Flambouro\, behind Profitis Ilias Apsilos: vespers and a morning panigiri on 17 July\, with the usual chickpea soup and lamb from the panigyras. Kamares (18 July) and Vathy (19 July) hold their own smaller Agia Marina feasts on the following nights\, so you can catch one each evening. It's reached on foot from the Apollonia–Profitis Ilias path\; wear proper shoes.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#flambouro-apollonia-area-panigiri-of-agia-marina-flambouro
